# PolySniffer Workspace — ONE Layout, Frozen Until v3

## Incident (2026-08-08, owner: Michael)

While onboarding a new external SaaS (Zoho) into PolySniffer, the agent built an
app-specific native-sniff processor that spliced the target site's own `<head>`
(including its full third-party CSS) into the shared workspace shell's `<head>`.
The target's CSS clobbered the shell's own `.btn` / `.toolbar` / `.split` rules —
toolbar buttons rendered as full-width stacked blocks instead of a compact row,
and the right-hand capture column disappeared. This broke the **same shared page
every tenant/every endpoint uses**, not just the one being onboarded — exactly
the failure mode this rule exists to prevent. The offending code was fully
removed (not patched, removed) the same session. See
`documentation/Capital Raise Project/` session notes / commit history around
2026-08-08 for the full incident trace.

## The One Rule

**There is exactly ONE PolySniffer workspace layout, shared by every endpoint,
every tenant, every mode (native and passthrough). It does not get a per-app
variant. It does not change to accommodate a specific SaaS's quirks. It is
frozen as of the 2026-06-24 "PolySniffer 2.0 Native Login Workspace" BINGO and
stays frozen until a deliberate, owner-approved v3.**

**AUTHORITATIVE files (the shared shell — the ONLY copies):**
- `dose/templates/polysniffer/sniff_workspace.html` — the shell itself: topbar,
  the two big mode cards (Native / Passthrough), the toolbar (Stop capture /
  Diff / Export HAR / Endpoints), the left browse pane, the right "Live
  capture" column. This is the file that must never change per-app.
- `dose/templates/polysniffer/sniff_workspace_capture.html` — content rendered
  inside the right-column capture iframe.
- `dose/templates/polysniffer/sniff_pt_orchestration_bar.html` — orchestration
  bar snippet for passthrough mode.
- `dose/polysniffer/views/sniff_v2_workspace.py` — the view that assembles
  context for the shell above.

Everything else under `dose/templates/polysniffer/` (`mode_picker.html`,
`dashboard.html`, `diff_view.html`, `sniff_native_embed.html`, and the
pre-2026-06-24 files like `sniffer.html`, `live_capture*.html`,
`in_content*.html`, `split_window.html`, `capture_interface.html`,
`building_pen_embed.html`) belongs to **other, separate routes** (endpoint
list, diff tool, legacy pre-v2 code) — not the workspace shell. Do not confuse
them with the one shell, and do not treat "it's a different template" as
license to introduce app-specific layout changes anywhere in this directory
without asking first.

## What broke it, and the actual rule that follows from it

The native/passthrough embed mechanism (`_extract_head_and_body` /
`build_inline_native_embed_context` in `dose/polysniffer/sniff_native_embed.py`)
splices an upstream app's own HTML `<head>`/`<body>` fragments directly into
`sniff_workspace.html`'s DOM. That means **any upstream app's CSS, if left
unfiltered, can leak into and break the shared shell** — this is a structural
risk for every future SaaS onboarded, not just Zoho.

- A new app's native-sniff processor (see `dose/polysniffer/handlers/*_native_sniff.py`,
  the Mattermost/HubSpot pattern) may rewrite that **app's own** response body.
  It must **never** assume it is safe to leave the target's global stylesheets
  in place once real content starts flowing through the splice point — verify
  with an actual screenshot (see `bingo-freeze.mdc` screenshot-proof rule)
  before trusting it, not just code review.
- If there is any doubt about whether a new integration's content is safe to
  splice into the shared shell, do not splice it. Fall back to the placeholder/
  unavailable state rather than risk the shared page for every tenant.
- Never touch `sniff_workspace.html`, `sniff_workspace_capture.html`,
  `sniff_pt_orchestration_bar.html`, or the workspace-assembly logic in
  `sniff_v2_workspace.py` while debugging a single app's onboarding. If the
  shared shell visibly changes as a side effect of onboarding one app, that is
  the bug — stop and revert the app-specific change, don't patch the shell.

## Before touching anything under `dose/templates/polysniffer/` or `dose/polysniffer/`

1. Identify whether the file is part of the ONE shared shell (list above) or a
   separate route. If it's the shared shell — assume it is correct and the bug
   is elsewhere, unless Michael/Shela explicitly say otherwise.
2. Get explicit approval before changing shared-shell behavior for any reason,
   including "just for testing."
3. After any change that *could* touch shared rendering (including adding a
   new native-sniff processor for a new app): restart, load the workspace for
   an *unrelated, already-working* endpoint (e.g. Odoo) first, screenshot it,
   and confirm it is pixel-identical to before. Only then test the new app.
4. Commit with a clear message; document with a screenshot per `bingo-freeze.mdc`.

## Do Not

- Add per-app CSS, per-app `<head>` content, or per-app layout branches to
  `sniff_workspace.html`.
- Assume a new native-sniff processor is safe because it "only touches that
  app's response body" — the response body is spliced into the shared page.
- Declare an onboarding fix done without a screenshot showing the shared shell
  (toolbar row, capture column) still renders correctly for a known-good app.
